# ENGINE_7 -- Revise

Command: `/revise-task`. Keep the slug. Follow
`.cursor/commands/revise-task.md` **and** this lane table.

## Lanes (order wins)

| Lane | When | Do | Do not |
|---|---|---|---|
| **O** oracle | Oracle 0, solve.sh broken | Fix derive-path, Dockerfile, pins | Ease tests, ENGINE_8 |
| **F** fairness | Unsolvable, hidden rules missing from `/app`, contradictory tests | Align docs and tests, oracle 1.0 | Instruction hints, drop hidden traps |
| **H** too easy | Probe saturated, visible-only would pass, one-file fix | **ENGINE_8** | This lane does not "add tests" |
| **R** reviewer | Solvable, comments only | FIX/IGNORE triage; bounce-risk first | Recipes, golden values, weakening hidden |
| **C** category/family | Wrong family for the work | Honest relabel or real restructure of all layers | Label-only novelty |

If Status is not solvable, **F beats R**. Do not produce an IGNORE table that
leaves unfair 0% tests.

## Outcome contract (LOCKED)

After the revision the task must still be:

- solvable (oracle 1.0)
- floored (NOP at declared floor)
- not one-shottable (probes V/D/L/A fail hidden)
- recipe-free instruction

Python-or-not does not change this. Odyssey has no `difficulty = "hard"`
key to relabel. Prose in `difficultyExplanation` is not hardness.

## Reviewer triage (lane R)

Safe FIX: docs match tests, harness, Dockerfile, fair contract wording that
does not give the recipe.

Forbidden FIX: checklists, bug file names, golden answers, dropping hidden
traps, visible weight raised so a shallow patch looks done.

```text
Trivial bounce risk: LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH -- <one fact>
Fixed: ...
Ignored: ... -- why: ...
```

HIGH -> do not zip. Prefer IGNORE on comments that would ease the probe.

